# Contents

Every card in this vault, in title order. Nobody maintains this list: the
cell below builds it, and the list you see is the output it saved. Open the
preview to read it, press **Code** to see the query, and **Run** to rebuild it.

```hql#eval id=books
cards
| filter(c => c.name != "contents")
| sort(by = c => c.title)
```
<!-- hql:output id=books hash=7282fba97096 status=ok -->
- [[dune]]
- [[emma]]
- [[middlemarch]]
- [[the-hobbit]]
<!-- /hql:output -->

## Still to read

A query cell runs so that other cells can read its value, and shows nothing of
its own — `hql#query` is `hql#eval hidden`. This one reads `books` and names
the result `todo`:

```hql#query id=todo
books | filter(c => c.metadata.status == "todo")
```

```hql#eval
todo | map(c => c.title)
```
<!-- hql:output hash=71e5d63fff98 status=ok -->
- Emma
- The Hobbit
<!-- /hql:output -->

## How far along

```hql#eval
{books: books | size, to_read: todo | size}
```
<!-- hql:output hash=779c4eb751ef status=ok -->
| key     | value |
| ------- | ----- |
| books   | 4     |
| to_read | 2     |
<!-- /hql:output -->

## A code listing is not a cell

A fence marked plain `hql` is shown as code and never runs:

```hql
cards | size
```
